XX. ☄️ R7.56 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

PRE-O01

A valid interpretation SHALL NOT automatically constitute precedent.

PRE-O02

Precedential status SHALL be explicitly representable.

PRE-O03

Precedential authority SHALL be separately attributable.

PRE-O04

Precedential scope SHALL be explicit.

PRE-O05

Precedential jurisdiction SHALL be explicit.

PRE-O06

Precedential epoch SHALL be explicit.

PRE-O07

Precedential force SHALL require constitutional basis.

PRE-O08

Majority preference SHALL NOT alone establish precedent.

PRE-O09

Recency SHALL NOT alone establish superior precedent.

PRE-O10

Authority over a determination SHALL NOT automatically confer precedential authority.

PRE-O11

Precedential core SHALL be distinguishable from incidental context.

PRE-O12

Precedential application SHALL remain within proven scope unless explicitly extended.

PRE-O13

Precedent extension SHALL require attributable authority.

PRE-O14

Precedent SHALL be distinguishable from precedent rejection.

PRE-O15

Precedent collision SHALL be explicitly detectable.

PRE-O16

Precedential supersession SHALL preserve historical lineage.

PRE-O17

Supersession SHALL NOT erase historical precedent.

PRE-O18

Cross-Citadel precedent SHALL NOT be silently treated as universally binding.

PRE-O19

Cross-Citadel precedential authority SHALL require explicit constitutional basis.

PRE-O20

ORACLE SHALL observe precedent creation and application.

PRE-O21

BRAINPOWER SHALL construct precedent graphs.

PRE-O22

FOOL SHALL challenge precedent capture and unauthorized extension.

PRE-O23

TRIAS SHALL determine precedential legitimacy within authorized jurisdiction.

PRE-O24

WATERMARK SHALL preserve precedential provenance.

PRE-O25

QUAY SHALL preserve precedent lineage.

PRE-O26

R5 SHALL replay precedential establishment and application.

PRE-O27

Historical precedent SHALL remain reconstructable after supersession.

PRE-O28

Precedential force SHALL remain distinguishable from semantic validity.

PRE-O29

A precedent SHALL NOT manufacture authority for the authority that created it.

PRE-O30

Self-authorizing precedent SHALL be rejected absent independent constitutional basis.

PRE-O31

Precedential conflict SHALL NOT be resolved solely through convenience.

PRE-O32

A precedent SHALL NOT automatically bind outside its jurisdiction.

PRE-O33

A precedent SHALL NOT automatically bind outside its semantic scope.

PRE-O34

Constitutional precedent SHALL be no stronger than its independently proven authority, scope, meaning and jurisdiction.


