XXIII. ☄️ R7.57 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

ACC-O01

Repeated precedent reliance SHALL NOT automatically constitute independent proof.

ACC-O02

Cumulative authority SHALL be distinguishable from cumulative evidence.

ACC-O03

Precedent dependency chains SHALL be explicitly representable.

ACC-O04

Independent proof anchors SHALL be distinguishable from inherited precedent references.

ACC-O05

Authority accretion SHALL be detectable.

ACC-O06

Precedent echo SHALL be detectable.

ACC-O07

Reference count SHALL NOT by itself establish constitutional authority.

ACC-O08

Reliance count SHALL NOT by itself establish constitutional legitimacy.

ACC-O09

Scope accretion SHALL be explicitly detectable.

ACC-O10

Jurisdictional accretion SHALL be explicitly detectable.

ACC-O11

Precedential authority SHALL NOT automatically expand through repeated use.

ACC-O12

Jurisprudential drift SHALL be detectable.

ACC-O13

Silent doctrinal mutation SHALL be detectable.

ACC-O14

Local semantic continuity SHALL NOT automatically establish global semantic continuity.

ACC-O15

Precedent composition SHALL be distinguishable from precedent citation.

ACC-O16

New constitutional propositions SHALL require their own proof basis.

ACC-O17

Composite precedent SHALL preserve all source lineage.

ACC-O18

Historical precedent SHALL remain observable after authority expansion or supersession.

ACC-O19

Authority level SHALL remain distinguishable from influence.

ACC-O20

Authority SHALL remain distinguishable from popularity.

ACC-O21

