ACC-O27

R5 SHALL replay authority growth and independent-support resolution.

ACC-O28

Scope extension SHALL require attributable constitutional basis.

ACC-O29

Jurisdictional extension SHALL require attributable constitutional basis.

ACC-O30

A precedent SHALL NOT become more constitutionally true merely because it is cited more often.

ACC-O31

A chain of dependent assertions SHALL NOT be treated as an equivalent number of independent proofs.

ACC-O32

Authority inherited from an unproven source SHALL remain unproven.

ACC-O33

Current doctrinal authority SHALL remain distinguishable from historical source authority.

ACC-O34

Constitutional authority SHALL be no stronger than the independently provable basis supporting its source, scope, jurisdiction, meaning and legitimacy.


