XXIV. ☄️ R7.65 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

CFI-O01

Constitutional state validity SHALL be distinguishable from interpretive frame validity.

CFI-O02

A determination SHALL identify its applicable constitutional frame.

CFI-O03

Constitutional frames SHALL be explicitly attributable.

CFI-O04

Frame succession SHALL be historically preserved.

CFI-O05

Rule identity SHALL be distinguishable from rule meaning.

CFI-O06

Meaning SHALL be temporally versionable.

CFI-O07

Current interpretation SHALL NOT silently rewrite historical meaning.

CFI-O08

Frame changes SHALL be explicitly detectable.

CFI-O09

Material frame shifts SHALL trigger appropriate revalidation.

CFI-O10

Frame validity SHALL require an independently attributable constitutional basis.

CFI-O11

A frame SHALL NOT derive authority solely from its own assertion.

CFI-O12

Frame jurisdiction SHALL be explicit.

CFI-O13

Cross-Citadel frame dependencies SHALL be explicit.

CFI-O14

Frame collision SHALL be distinguishable from state conflict.

CFI-O15

Historical determinations SHALL retain their original frame.

CFI-O16

Historical meaning SHALL remain observable after frame succession.

CFI-O17

Retroactive reinterpretation SHALL require explicit constitutional authorization.

CFI-O18

ORACLE SHALL observe semantic and frame drift.

CFI-O19

BRAINPOWER SHALL construct frame dependency graphs.

CFI-O20

FOOL SHALL challenge frame self-authorization and semantic erasure.

CFI-O21

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional frame validity and succession.

CFI-O22

WATERMARK SHALL preserve frame provenance.

CFI-O23

QUAY SHALL preserve frame lineage.

CFI-O24

R5 SHALL replay historical frame and meaning context.

CFI-O25

A valid state SHALL NOT imply permanent meaning stability.

CFI-O26

A valid evidence object SHALL NOT imply permanent interpretive meaning.

CFI-O27

Same rule text SHALL NOT automatically imply same interpretation across epochs.

CFI-O28

Frame-relative validity SHALL remain temporally and jurisdictionally attributable.

CFI-O29

Frame shifts SHALL NOT erase previous frames.

CFI-O30

A current frame SHALL NOT retrospectively canonicalize its own interpretation.

CFI-O31

Frame compatibility SHALL be explicitly determined.

CFI-O32

Meaning equivalence SHALL be distinguished from rule identity.

CFI-O33

Semantic drift SHALL be independently observable.

CFI-O34

Constitutional meaning SHALL remain attributable to its applicable frame and epoch.


---

XXV. ☄️ R7.65 EQUATION

Constitutional determination:

D =
STATE
+
RULE
+
FRAME
+
INTERPRETATION
+
EVIDENCE
+
AUTHORITY
+
JURISDICTION
+
TIME

Frame-relative validity:

VALIDITY =
STATE
|
FRAME
|
TIME
|
JURISDICTION

Meaning:

MEANING(R,T,F,J)

Dus:

R₁ = R₁

kan bestaan naast:

MEANING(R₁,T₁,F₁,J)
≠
MEANING(R₁,T₂,F₂,J)

Zonder dat de historische rule identity noodzakelijk verloren gaat.

De kernregel:

SAME RULE DOES NOT GUARANTEE SAME MEANING.

En nog dieper:

SAME STATE DOES NOT GUARANTEE SAME CONSTITUTIONAL FRAME.


