II. 🧬 COMPOSITIONAL CONSTITUTIONALITY

R7.70 defines:

COMPOSITIONAL_CONSTITUTIONALITY

as:

> the independently established constitutional validity of a combined state, action, authority structure or interaction resulting from the composition of otherwise individually valid components.



Formally:

C(A) ∧ C(B)

does not entail:

C(A ⊕ B)

The composition itself becomes a constitutional object.


---

III. 🔱 INTERACTION EFFECT

R7.70 introduces:

INTERACTION_EFFECT

An interaction effect occurs when the combined behavior of two or more constitutional objects produces a property that cannot be established merely by independently examining those objects.

Conceptually:

A → effect(A)
B → effect(B)

A ⊕ B → effect(A,B)

where:

effect(A,B)

may differ materially from:

effect(A) + effect(B)

This is the beginning of:

EMERGENT CONSTITUTIONAL BEHAVIOR.


---

