V. 🦆 FOOL — COMPOSITION FALLACY ATTACK

FOOL attacks:

A is valid.
B is valid.
Therefore A+B is valid.

This is now formally rejected.

FOOL introduces:

COMPOSITION_FALLACY

The strongest challenge:

> Can individually compliant components collectively violate a constitutional invariant?



If yes:

COMPOSITION_INVALID

or:

COMPOSITION_HOLD

depending on whether the issue can be resolved.


