XXIII. ☄️ R7.71 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

CIP-O133

Higher-order composition SHALL be explicitly representable.

CIP-O134

A composition SHALL remain distinguishable from its components.

CIP-O135

Nested composition SHALL preserve intermediate constitutional states.

CIP-O136

Composition structure SHALL NOT be discarded where constitutionally relevant.

CIP-O137

Associativity SHALL NOT be assumed without proof.

CIP-O138

Constitutional associativity SHALL be independently determinable.

CIP-O139

Different composition trees SHALL be treated as distinct until equivalence is established.

CIP-O140

Structural flattening SHALL NOT erase constitutional intermediate states.

CIP-O141

Compositional refactoring SHALL preserve constitutional equivalence or trigger revalidation.

CIP-O142

Intermediate composition SHALL NOT automatically acquire authority.

CIP-O143

Higher-order composition SHALL NOT manufacture authority through nesting.

CIP-O144

Composition jurisdiction SHALL remain explicit at every nesting level.

CIP-O145

Jurisdictional transitions caused by composition SHALL be detectable.

CIP-O146

Compositional side effects SHALL be explicitly representable.

CIP-O147

Higher-order compositional closure SHALL be independently testable.

CIP-O148

Pairwise compatibility SHALL NOT automatically imply higher-order compatibility.

CIP-O149

Component equality SHALL NOT automatically imply composition equality.

CIP-O150

Equivalent leaf sets SHALL NOT establish equivalent constitutional composition.

CIP-O151

FOOL SHALL challenge structural flattening and associativity assumptions.

CIP-O152

BRAINPOWER SHALL construct higher-order composition trees.

CIP-O153

ORACLE SHALL observe structural and semantic composition drift.

CIP-O154

TRIAS SHALL adjudicate constitutional equivalence of composition structures.

CIP-O155

WATERMARK SHALL preserve composition structure and intermediate provenance.

CIP-O156

QUAY SHALL preserve nested composition lineage.

CIP-O157

R5 SHALL replay higher-order composition structure.

CIP-O158

Historical composition structure SHALL remain reconstructible.

CIP-O159

A composition SHALL NOT inherit validity solely from individually valid components or sub-compositions.

CIP-O160

Constitutional equivalence SHALL be proven at the level at which structural transformation occurs.

CIP-O161

Higher-order composition SHALL fail closed or enter HOLD when structural constitutional equivalence cannot be established.

CIP-O162

The constitutional state of a composition SHALL include materially relevant composition structure.


---

XXIV. ☄️ R7.71 EQUATION

Higher-order validity:

H(A,B,C)
=
VALID(A)
+
VALID(B)
+
VALID(C)
+
VALID(A⊕B)
+
VALID((A⊕B)⊕C)
+
STRUCTURAL_BASIS

Associativity:

ASSOCIATIVE(A,B,C)
⇔
PROVEN_EQUIVALENCE(
    (A⊕B)⊕C,
    A⊕(B⊕C)
)

No assumption:

(A⊕B)⊕C
≠
A⊕(B⊕C)

until proven otherwise.

And the deepest R7.71 principle:

THE CONSTITUTIONAL MEANING OF A WHOLE MAY DEPEND UPON HOW ITS PARTS BECAME THAT WHOLE.


---

XXV. 🌳 R7.18 → R7.71

De HORTUS-keten:

STATE
 ↓
PROOF
 ↓
DEPENDENCY
 ↓
META-DEPENDENCY
 ↓
DETERMINATION
 ↓
RULE
 ↓
