XI. 🧩 SEMANTIC CONTINUITY

A domain can remain structurally similar while its meaning changes.

Therefore R7.73 introduces:

SEMANTIC_PROOF_CONTINUITY

A proof may continue only when the semantics relevant to its validity remain preserved.

Conceptually:

STRUCTURE
   +
SEMANTICS
   +
INVARIANTS
   +
BOUNDARIES

must remain sufficiently aligned.

Thus:

STRUCTURAL_EQUIVALENCE
        ≠
SEMANTIC_EQUIVALENCE

and:

SEMANTIC_CHANGE
        ≠
AUTOMATIC INVALIDITY

but:

MATERIAL_SEMANTIC_CHANGE
        →
REVALIDATION


