I. ☄️ THE NEXT BOUNDARY

R7.73 established:

D₁
 ↓ evolution
D₂
 ↓
PROOF CONTINUITY?

and rejected automatic inheritance.

But R7.73 leaves an even deeper problem:

WHO PROVES THAT THE PROOF DOMAIN
IS STILL CAPABLE OF PROVING ITSELF?

A proof domain may evolve.

Its invariants may evolve.

Its proof predicate may evolve.

Its certificate machinery may evolve.

Its own validator may evolve.

Therefore:

PROOF DOMAIN
     ↓
SELF-REVISION
     ↓
NEW PROOF DOMAIN
     ↓
VALIDATION OF NEW PROOF DOMAIN

creates the possibility of a circular claim:

> “The new proof system says that the new proof is valid.”



R7.74 therefore establishes:

PROOF OF PROOF MUST NOT DEPEND UPON UNCHECKED SELF-ASSERTION.


