II. 🌱 CONSTITUTIONAL PLURALISM

R7.76 defines:

CONSTITUTIONAL_PLURALISM

as:

> the capacity of a federation to preserve multiple independently legitimate constitutional frameworks without automatically collapsing them into a single universal authority or declaring one framework universally superior.



Therefore:

VALID(A)
∧
VALID(B)

does not imply:

A = B

Nor:

A > B

Nor:

A ⊕ B = NEW_TRUTH

Instead:

A ───────── VALID WITHIN DOMAIN A
B ───────── VALID WITHIN DOMAIN B


---

III. 🧭 CONSTITUTIONAL DOMAIN SEPARATION

Every constitutional framework receives an explicit domain:

CONSTITUTION_A {
    jurisdiction = J_A
    authority = AUTH_A
    scope = S_A
    epoch = E_A
}

and:

CONSTITUTION_B {
    jurisdiction = J_B
    authority = AUTH_B
    scope = S_B
    epoch = E_B
}

The federation must first determine:

J_A ∩ J_B
S_A ∩ S_B
AUTH_A ∩ AUTH_B
E_A ∩ E_B

before attempting reconciliation.

This creates the first rule:

CONFLICT REQUIRES OVERLAP.

If two constitutional domains never overlap:

A ∩ B = ∅

there may be no constitutional conflict at all.


---

