XIX. 🦆 FOOL — INTERSECTION FALLACY

FOOL attacks:

> “Both constitutions permit X, therefore the federation has authority over X.”



Rejected.

It attacks:

> “The intersection exists, therefore the federation owns the intersection.”



Rejected.

It attacks:

> “The federation coordinated the agreement, therefore federation authority was created.”



Rejected.

Thus:

COORDINATION DOES NOT CREATE AUTHORITY.

Authority must already exist or be constitutionally delegated.


