But a deeper phenomenon can occur.

Suppose:

A + B

produces a state that possesses properties that neither A nor B possessed independently.

Then:

A ≠ S
B ≠ S
A ⊕ B = S

where S is genuinely new.

The critical question becomes:

> Is S merely a composition of existing constitutional states, or has a new constitutional object come into existence?



R7.77 establishes the distinction.

EMERGENT_CONSTITUTIONAL_STATE


