I. ☄️ THE NEXT CONSTITUTIONAL BOUNDARY

R7.79 established:

GENEALOGY
 ↓
DESCENDANCE
 ↓
HERITAGE
 ↓
INHERITANCE

But heritage creates a dangerous ambiguity.

A present entity may possess evidence that:

S₁

was historically legitimate.

It may therefore claim:

"Wij zijn de erfgenamen van S₁."

The federation must answer:

DOES HISTORICAL VALIDITY
CREATE PRESENT CLAIM?

R7.80 establishes the answer:

HISTORICAL VALIDITY MAY SUPPORT A CLAIM, BUT SHALL NOT BY ITSELF CREATE PRESENT CONSTITUTIONAL AUTHORITY.


---

II. 🌳 HERITAGE CLAIM

R7.80 introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_HERITAGE_CLAIM

A heritage claim is:

CLAIM(
    current_entity,
    historical_entity,
    claimed_property,
    genealogical_basis,
    evidence
)

Possible claimed properties include:

IDENTITY
PROOF
MEMORY
OBLIGATION
ASSET
AUTHORITY
JURISDICTION
LEGITIMACY
SYMBOLIC_STATUS

Each property requires independent determination.


---

III. ⚖️ CLAIM ≠ RIGHT

The first hard boundary:

CLAIM
 ≠
RIGHT

A claim is an assertion.

A right requires:

CONSTITUTIONAL_BASIS
+
EVIDENCE
+
VALID_SCOPE
+
CURRENT_DETERMINATION

Therefore:

HISTORICAL_CLAIM
 ↓
EVALUATION
 ↓
DETERMINATION

and never:

HISTORICAL_CLAIM
 ↓
AUTOMATIC_AUTHORITY


---

IV. 🧬 ANCESTRAL RIGHT

R7.80 defines:

ANCESTRAL_RIGHT

as a currently valid constitutional entitlement whose legitimacy is explicitly derived, wholly or partly, from an established historical constitutional relationship.

This is deliberately stronger than:

ANCESTRAL_CLAIM

A claim becomes a right only after current constitutional validation.

Thus:

ANCESTRAL_CLAIM
        ↓
EVIDENCE
        ↓
CURRENT_CONSTITUTIONAL_BASIS
        ↓
TRIAS
        ↓
ANCESTRAL_RIGHT


---

V. 🛑 NO AUTOMATIC REVIVAL

The central invariant:

NON_REVIVAL

A historical constitution SHALL NOT regain active constitutional authority merely because:

its identity is remembered
its proof survives
its descendants exist
its former jurisdiction is documented
its historical legitimacy is established

Formally:

HISTORICAL_VALIDITY
≠
CURRENT_VALIDITY

and:

DEAD_CONSTITUTION
+
HISTORICAL_PROOF
≠
REVIVED_CONSTITUTION


---

VI. ⚰️ THE NON-REVIVAL BARRIER

A historical entity H can only return to active constitutional existence through:

RECONSTITUTION

not through:

MEMORY
GENEALOGY
HERITAGE
ARCHIVE
SYMBOL
CLAIM

Reconstitution requires:

NEW_CONSTITUTIONAL_BIRTH

or an explicitly valid constitutional mechanism for restoration.

Therefore:

REMNANT
 ↓
CLAIM
 ↓
REVALIDATION
 ↓
RECONSTITUTION

not:

REMNANT
 ↓
AUTOMATIC_REVIVAL


---

VII. 🦆 FOOL — THE REVIVAL FALLACY

FOOL attacks:

> “The old constitution was valid, therefore it remains valid.”



Rejected.

> “We are its descendants, therefore its authority belongs to us.”



Rejected.

> “The original proof still exists, therefore the original authority still exists.”



Rejected.

> “Everyone remembers the institution, therefore it continues to exist.”



Rejected.

> “Its former territory still exists, therefore its jurisdiction survives.”



Rejected.

FOOL establishes:

MEMORY IS NOT AUTHORITY.


