FORBIDDEN
UNKNOWN


---

IX. 💧 WATERMARK — CLAIM PROVENANCE

WATERMARK records:

W_HERITAGE_CLAIM {
    claim_id
    claimant_entity
    historical_entity
    claimed_property
    genealogical_basis
    evidence_set
    historical_epoch
    current_epoch
    jurisdiction
    constitutional_basis
    challenge_set
    determination_id
    status
    provenance
}

Thus a verifier can reconstruct:

> Why does this entity claim this heritage?



and:

> What evidence supports the claim?



and most importantly:

> What prevents the claim from becoming unauthorized authority?




---

X. ⚓ QUAY — MEMORY WITHOUT AUTHORITY

QUAY stores historical heritage claims separately from active authority.

HISTORICAL_LEDGER
        │
        ├── EVENTS
        ├── PROOFS
        ├── ENTITIES
        ├── SUCCESSIONS
        └── CLAIMS
                 │
                 ║
                 ║  ← CONSTITUTIONAL FIREWALL
                 ║
                 ↓
          ACTIVE AUTHORITY

Historical storage therefore becomes:

NON_AUTHORITY_PRESERVING_STORAGE

The archive remembers.

It does not govern.


---

XI. 👑 L.A. — MEMORY ARCHITECTURE

L.A. now separates:

👑 L.A.
                       │
                    HORTUS
                       │
          ┌────────────┴────────────┐
          ↓                         ↓
    LIVING CONSTITUTION       HISTORICAL MEMORY
          │                         │
       AUTHORITY                 EVIDENCE
          │                         │
     JURISDICTION               HERITAGE
          │                         │
