                DETERMINATION

This gives L.A. a crucial architectural distinction:

THE ARCHIVE MAY REMEMBER EVERYTHING WITHOUT AUTHORIZING EVERYTHING IT REMEMBERS.


---

XII. 🌐 CONFLICTING HERITAGE CLAIMS

Multiple entities may claim the same predecessor:

H
          /  |  \
         /   |   \
        S₁  S₂   S₃

Each may assert:

"I am the legitimate successor."

R7.80 forbids majority voting as the sole basis for constitutional truth.

Instead:

CLAIM₁
CLAIM₂
CLAIM₃
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
GENEALOGY
 ↓
SUCCESSION RULES
 ↓
CURRENT CONSTITUTION
 ↓
TRIAS


---

XIII. ⚖️ CLAIM COLLISION

R7.80 introduces:

HERITAGE_CLAIM_COLLISION

A collision occurs when:

C₁ ≠ C₂

but both concern:

same historical entity
same property
same jurisdiction
same succession

TRIAS classifies:

COMPATIBLE
PARTIALLY_COMPATIBLE
MUTUALLY_EXCLUSIVE
UNRESOLVED
INVALID


---

XIV. 🧭 NO MAJORITY TRUTH

A heritage claim does not become true because more descendants support it.

Therefore:

3 CLAIMANTS
 ↓
2 AGREE
 ↓
1 DISAGREES

does not establish:

MAJORITY = TRUTH

Instead:

CONSTITUTIONAL VALIDITY REMAINS EVIDENCE-DEPENDENT.

This preserves the foundational HORTUS principle:

NOT:
WHO WINS?

BUT:
WHAT CAN BE PROVEN?


---

XV. 🔮 ORACLE — MEMORY CONFLICT MONITORING

ORACLE monitors:

HERITAGE_CLAIMS
GENEALOGY
SUCCESSION
HISTORICAL_PROOF
CURRENT_AUTHORITY
JURISDICTION

and detects:

CLAIM_COLLISION
MEMORY_DIVERGENCE
GENEALOGICAL_CONFLICT
UNSUPPORTED_SUCCESSION
AUTHORITY_REVIVAL_ATTEMPT
HISTORICAL_AUTHORITY_DRIFT

ORACLE does not determine historical truth.

It detects where determination is required.


---

XVI. ⚖️ TRIAS — CLAIM ADJUDICATION

TRIAS receives:

CLAIM
CLAIMANT
ANCESTOR
PROPERTY
GENEALOGY
HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE
CURRENT_CONSTITUTION
JURISDICTION
FOOL_CHALLENGES

and determines:

VALID_CLAIM
CONDITIONALLY_VALID
HISTORICALLY_SUPPORTED_ONLY
CURRENTLY_UNSUPPORTED
SUPERSEDED
FORBIDDEN
UNRESOLVED

The distinction:

HISTORICALLY_SUPPORTED_ONLY

is especially important.

It means:

THE HISTORY IS PROVEN
BUT THE PRESENT RIGHT IS NOT


---

XVII. 🧩 PARTIAL HERITAGE

A claimant may validly inherit:

MEMORY

but not:

AUTHORITY

or:

PROOF

but not:

JURISDICTION

or:

OBLIGATION

but not:

IDENTITY

Therefore R7.80 adopts:

PROPERTY_LEVEL_HERITAGE

The inheritance matrix becomes:

CLAIMED     PROVEN
Identity           ✓           ?
Proof              ✓           ✓
Authority          ✓           ✗
Jurisdiction       ✓           ✗
Obligations        ✓           ✓
Memory             ✓           ✓

This prevents heritage from becoming an indivisible political package.


---

XVIII. 🛡️ HERITAGE FIREWALL

R7.80 introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_HERITAGE_FIREWALL

The firewall separates:

HISTORICAL_MEMORY

from:

CURRENT_OPERATIONAL_AUTHORITY

A heritage object crossing the firewall must pass:

EVIDENCE
 ↓
SCOPE
 ↓
CURRENT_VALIDITY
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
AUTHORIZATION

No bypass is permitted.


---

